WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.601
-Our next guest
is a talented actor

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.104
who stars in the Netflix series
"The Woman in the House

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.740
Across the Street
from the Girl in the Window."

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.909
All eight episodes
will be available to stream

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.245
on Netflix starting tomorrow.
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.215
-Is there anything I can do?

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.849
-Like what?

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:18.851
-Build a time machine
so you can go back in time

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:21.821
and change things.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.456
-Hi, Anna.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.058
-Hi, Emma.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.459
-All right.
We should go.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.695
It's good seeing you.
-W-Wait, one second.

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:32.565
I want you to have this.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:36.869
Life is for the living.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:38.771
And so are casseroles.

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:40.739
[ Laughter ]
-Please welcome to the show

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.108
Tom Riley, everybody!

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.610
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:54.620 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.491 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.491
How are you, Tom?

00:00:59.491 --> 00:01:01.060
-I'm good, I'm good.
Thank you.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.729
-I'm very happy
to have you here.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.964
Your talented wife,
the actress Lizzy Caplan,

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.066
has been here in the past.
She's back in the green room.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.168
It was lovely to see her.
-Thank you.

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:12.105
When my name is mentioned,
when she says

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.207
that she's married to me,
the type of applause

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.375
that I get -- that she gets
is more the sort of,

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.345
"Oh, well done. You've fostered
an old stray dog."

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.346
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.615
-But that --
She deserves that.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.683
She's the best.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.050
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
-Yeah, it's right.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.752
They're like,
"That's so sweet of you, Lizzy,

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.187
to have done that."
-Yeah, thank you.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.690
-How are you guys doing?
-We're good.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.325
We --
We just had a baby.

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:35.695
-You did!
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.796
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.497
-Now, is this one of these --

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:40.065
Is this one of these
secret babies?

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:42.635
-Yeah, I mean, we say --
Yeah, I say we just had a baby.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:45.304
It was -- It was about
4 1/2 months ago.

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:47.340
Someone else said --
the other day they said,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.143
"Is this -- Did you do this --
Was this a secret pregnancy?"

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:54.847
And, I mean, not on purpose.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:57.450
-It's just we didn't --
We didn't tell anyone.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.518
It's not like we --
we snuck Lizzy into the hospital

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:01.988
under a blanket,
and then, two days later,

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:06.493
we, like, emerge with a baby
hidden in a bowling-ball bag.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.428
We just -- We just --
No one asked.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.629
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.431
-So we just, you know --
-Well, congratulations.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.500
Have you -- how has fatherhood
treated you so far?

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.069
-It is -- It's good.
-Yeah.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:19.205
-Yeah. It's --
No, it's great.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.606
-You know what?
I'm sorry.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:22.475
"Good" is the honest answer,
and I really appreciated it.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.676
-Thank you, thank you.
-Let's not go crazy.

00:02:24.676 --> 00:02:26.879
-It has its ups and downs.
-It has its ups and downs.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:30.516
And at 4 months old,
they are, you know...

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.718
-They're a little something.
-There's not a lot going on.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:36.289
-No, well, that's the thing.
And we had him in London.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.725
-Mm-hmm.
-But we -- Yeah, so we

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.192
flew back here
when he was 3 months old.

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:42.228
And have you --
You've just had --

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.063
-Yeah, but we have not
put her on an airplane yet.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.532
-Have you done an international
flight with a young...?

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.734
-Not that young.
No, that's young, too.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.737
-Everyone said to us,
"It's young, but it's okay.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.438
They're gonna sleep
the whole way."

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.173
-Right.
-That is not true.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.775
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:58.144
And the thing about babies --
I don't know.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.079
This may come
as a surprise to you,

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.181
but they [bleep] themselves...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:04.617
...and they don't care
where they are.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.319
-Right.
-They don't care if they're

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.087
on the ground
or if they're in the air.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.121
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:10.923
-But we were so prepared.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:14.126
We had, like, a go bag.
-Yes.

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:15.494
-Like doomsday preppers.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.429
It was, like, full of, like,
diapers and everything.

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:19.832
But we put it up
in the overhead compartment.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:23.336
And what no one said is that,
on takeoff,

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.571
it's not just their ears
that pop.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:26.705
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:28.941
It's also their buttholes.
That's right.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:34.180
And so we get to like
5,000 feet, and he looks at us,

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.049
and he just sort of goes
that kind of red

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.818
from the neck up
that means he's, like...

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.886
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.520
-...cooking a fresh batch
or something.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.789
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.557
-And we're just like,
"Don't you -- Don't you --

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:48.361
Not now. Don't --"
And he just -- bfff!

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.495
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.431
I mean, like --
like a confetti cannon.

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.665
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:55.468
Like, we're celebrating
something awful.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.169
And it goes, like,
through his --

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:58.471
through his clothes,
through his diaper.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:01.106
Like, somehow
it's in his hair instantly.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:03.609
And everyone around us
is going like, "Oh, no.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:04.910
Oh, no, no."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.746
-"We're stuck on the plane
with this baby."

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.847
And I don't know.

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:13.819
I felt like this may not be the
case for you, but, like, I --

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.656
Being a new daddy, there's
a lot of feeling very useless.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.257
-Yes, 100%.
-Most of the beginning.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.259
-Yeah.
-And so anytime I can see a job

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:22.095
that I can do, I'm like,
"That's -- I'm here.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.197
I'm ready."
-Oh, that's very noble, yeah.

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.865
-And I felt like,
"Operation Clean Up --

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.333
I've got this."
-Yeah.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:30.536
-And the minute those seatbelt
signs go out, I am going to --

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.705
I'm gonna get these guys
to the bathroom.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:35.741
So, I'm there like, "8,000 feet,
9,000 feet, 10,000 feet."

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:37.877
Seatbelts --
the seatbelt sign goes out.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.379
I'm, like, up on the aisle.
"Make way!

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:45.117
Lady with -- lady with baby!
Lady with a stinky baby!"

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.987
And --
And we go into the bathroom.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.455
Oh, she's gonna kill me
for telling this,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.491
I've just realized, this story.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:55.962
Um...
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.564
-Well, it's not like -- it's not
like you're that far into it.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.032
-No, you're right.
You're right.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:03.436
[ Laughter ]
Okay.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:08.040
And -- And so we get in there,
or Lizzy goes in ahead,

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.110
and she puts Alfie --
is our son -- down on the --

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.746
on the toilet, basically, 'cause
it's a tiny airplane bathroom.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.581
I try and get in there.
I can't get in.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.849
Like, "What can I do?
How can I help?"

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.284
And she's like, "Just stay --
stay on the door.

00:05:19.284 --> 00:05:20.853
Make sure no one comes in.
It can't lock.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.454
Just stay there."
I'm like, "I've got it.

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:24.056
Daddy's here.
Daddy's here.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:25.591
Everybody's safe."

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:28.226
And I stand there
thinking I'm gonna be

00:05:28.226 --> 00:05:30.730
an impenetrable wall.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.132
And then, the seatbelt sign
comes back on.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:34.600
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.670
and I'm a stickler
for the rules.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.172
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:43.375
You know, especially the rules
of -- the law of the sky.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:44.410
-Sure, of course.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.078
They can pull
your flight status.

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:47.980
-Exactly. And anyone could've
been an air marshal.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.081
-Right.
-I don't know.

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:50.616
[ Laughter ]
And so I was like,

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.218
"Well, if I go back down,
no one's gonna --

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.052
no one's gonna come and --"
-Right.

00:05:54.052 --> 00:05:56.455
-"The seatbelt sign's on.
No one's gonna interrupt her.

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:58.090
So I went, and I sat,
and I unclip --

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.893
clipped my belt back on.
And I look,

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:04.463
and this guy gets up, and he
starts to walk to the thing,

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.666
and I'm like, "Don't, don't,
don't, no, no, no, no, no!"

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:10.202
And he opens the door,
and he gasps, and Lizzy --

00:06:10.202 --> 00:06:12.271
I can still --
I can still see it.

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.406
Like, because of the way
she's positioned,

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:17.109
she's on all fours,
and she's got, like,

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:21.380
poop up her arms,
maybe a little bit on her face.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.581
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:24.616
-And because of the way
she's there on all fours

00:06:24.616 --> 00:06:27.019
in front of the toilet,
you can't even see the baby.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.788
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:33.092
And it -- it just looks like
she's eating out of the toilet.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.328
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:38.231
And, I mean, I felt embarrassed.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:40.132
I felt regret.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:43.001
-I felt like I was --
I hadn't protected my family.

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:45.771
-Did you feel like opening
the door and just jumping?

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:46.939
-Yeah!
But that was the thing.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.273
I'm stuck.
I can't escape.

00:06:48.273 --> 00:06:50.275
I say there's nowhere I can go.
My wife's mad at me.

00:06:50.275 --> 00:06:53.412
And that is basically what being
a dad feels like it's all about.

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:56.015
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:57.816
-The effort!

00:06:57.816 --> 00:07:00.386
The fact that you made
the effort.

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.221
Real quick,
because I will not --

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.622
I had to read it off cue cards.

00:07:03.622 --> 00:07:05.358
So, this show that you're in
with Kristen Bell,

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:08.727
which is a sort of parody
of sorts of this kind of

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.929
crime thriller that we've
sort of fallen in love with

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:13.465
the last few years, how --

00:07:13.465 --> 00:07:14.867
Can you say the title
real quick,

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:16.635
and how long did it take you
to learn it?

00:07:16.635 --> 00:07:18.171
-"The Woman in the House
Across the Street

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:19.672
from the Girl in the Window"?
-Yeah.

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.173
-We had a little head start
because it was called

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:22.507
"The Woman in the House"
when we were shooting it,

00:07:22.507 --> 00:07:24.877
and that's sort of 40%.
So when they added the rest,

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.145
I already had that
in my back pocket.

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:28.247
-Right.
-It was down, yeah.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:29.749
-Well, it's really fun.
And you and Kristen

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.650
are great together, and thank
you so much for being here.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:32.984
What a pleasure to have you.
-Oh, such a pleasure.

00:07:32.984 --> 00:07:34.720
-You guys, that's Tom Riley.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.422
"The Woman in the House
Across the Street

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.890
from the Girl in the Window"
is available to stream

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.225
on Netflix starting tomorrow.

